    "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `verify_splitkv.py`, stage 1 marks an inactive split by writing `-inf` to its LSE, but it never writes that split's `Att_Out`. Stage 2 still loads the scratch and multiplies it by a zero weight, so a NaN left over in the buffer turns into a NaN in the output (0 × NaN = NaN). Separately, when every prefix split is empty, `exp(-inf - (-inf))` is itself NaN.\n\nI haven't seen this happen on its own in a running server, but it reproduces every time the scratch holds NaN. The output shouldn't depend on what an unused buffer happened to contain.\n\n## Changes\n\nAll in `_verify_combine_stage2`:\n\n- skip the load for splits whose LSE is `-inf`;\n- if every split is empty, use zero weights and guard the 0/0.\n\nNo extra memory and no change to the launch config.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe new test fills the scratch with NaN, then checks a 1-token prefix and an empty prefix (expected 3/4/5 and 4/5/6) in both eager mode and CUDA graph replay. On main, all 12,288 outputs are NaN for the 1-token case. With this change `test_verify_splitkv.py` passes 10/10 on H20.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis kernel is only dispatched on gfx95 today. #39316 would turn it on for CUDA by default, which makes this hardening matter more. cc @HaiShaw @chuyeh @1am9trash\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39247491647](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39247491647)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39247491801](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39247491801)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39247491695](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39247491695)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
